  m_Name: Forest_ExpertAdvice_1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Game.Collectable.CollectableItem
  id: Forest_ExpertAdvice_1
  headerName: "Expert Field Notes \u2014 Surviving a Dry Landslide"
  content: "Should you face a <b><color=#C60004>dry landslide </color></b>, survival
    depends on reading the physical signs and escaping the direction of movement.\n\n<size=120%><b>1.
    Escape</b></size>\n\n* <color=#cc6600><b>Run laterally:</b></color> If you see
    earth or stone beginning to move, flee perpendicular to the slide. Never run
    downhill in the same direction \u2014 the slide will outrun you.\n* <color=#cc6600><b>Move
    toward stable high ground:</b></color> Solid rock or a firm ridgeline is your
    destination.\n* <color=#cc6600><b>Do not shelter behind trees: </b></color>In
    a dry slide, the impact force can fell them onto you. Find a large deeply-anchored
    boulder or solid structure instead.\n\n\r<size=120%><b>2. Warning Signs</b></size>\n\n*
    <color=#cc6600><b>Unusual sounds: </b></color> stones striking each other, the
    sharp cracking of branches, or a deep rumbling from beneath the earth like a
    freight train underground.\n* <color=#cc6600><b>Fresh fissures: </b></color>
    new cracks appearing on the trail surface or along the hillside.\n* <color=#cc6600><b>Dust
    rising from the slope without any wind: </color></b> That means the earth is
    already beginning to move.\n\n<size=120%><b>3. Safe Ground</b></size>\n\n* <color=#cc6600><b>Avoid
    narrow gullies:</b></color> Debris flows into low channels. Stay clear of them
    even in bright sunlight."
  type: 0
  biome: 0
  icon: {fileID: 0}
  dialogData: {fileID: 0}
